{"content":[{"c":["ASHER (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Jacob’s son born to Leah’s maid Zilpah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.30.12-13","r":"Gen.30.12-13","rawR":"Gen.30.12-13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.30.12-13","value":"Gen.30.12-13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 30:12-13"},"). The name Asher, probably meaning “happy,” was given to the child by Leah in her delight at his birth. Asher had four sons, Imnah, Ishvah, Ishvi, and Beriah, and a daughter, Serah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.17","r":"Gen.46.17","rawR":"Gen.46.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.17","value":"Gen.46.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.7.30","r":"1Chr.7.30","rawR":"1Chr.7.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.7.30","value":"1Chr.7.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 7:30"},"). Some have speculated that the tribe of Asher took its name from a locality mentioned in Egyptian texts of the 13th century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". It is more likely that the tribe bore the name of its ancestor. Asher and his brothers received a special blessing and prediction from Jacob as he was dying (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.49.20","r":"Gen.49.20","rawR":"Gen.49.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.49.20","value":"Gen.49.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 49:20"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.33.24-25","r":"Deut.33.24-25","rawR":"Deut.33.24-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.33.24-25","value":"Deut.33.24-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 33:24-25"},", where the dying Moses blessed Asher and the other tribes)."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=AsherTribe_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"AsherTribe_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"AsherTribe_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Asher (Tribe)"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AsherPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 30:12-13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.30.12-13","rawQueryValue":"Gen.30.12-13","sourceRefExact":"Gen.30.12-13"},{"anchorText":"Gn 46:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.17","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.17","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 7:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.7.30","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.7.30","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.7.30"},{"anchorText":"Gn 49:20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.49.20","rawQueryValue":"Gen.49.20","sourceRefExact":"Gen.49.20"},{"anchorText":"Dt 33:24-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.33.24-25","rawQueryValue":"Deut.33.24-25","sourceRefExact":"Deut.33.24-25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2cd13745b0f417ec7264e919d98e64c876b3e19a98d710bf78c954a9398ced87","sourceItemName":"AsherPerson","sourceItemOrder":538,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"AsherPerson","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Asher (Person)","title":"Asher (Person)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}